9","maturity":"draft","page_type":"entity","path":"pages/entities/codehamr-codehamr-e5c59fb56649.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":[],"title":"codehamr/codehamr","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:43:04Z","updated_by_operation":"op_2ac18e71bbde44e7aa1191650fd2bed7"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_06731ae1bf9be4a80775b4297bb526d6fb1627e95041a92d7607ce640c091bd7"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"codehamr is described as a minimal coding agent for the terminal, built for local LLMs and also able to run against OpenAI-compatible endpoints."},{"claim_ids":["clm_1ac704a82a26b8e0a4489f382f603a83766291ab2e253241b2d269c3a8642a83"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Because Ollama's /v1 endpoint reports no context-window header, codehamr packs to the configured context_size; if the server honors less, it silently front-truncates and the agent can lose its system prompt and earlier tool results mid-task with no error."},{"claim_ids":["clm_2175083c3dcb190b435d97a079ae4d1c8d53512ea22eeb5b7e106169d2c8cc18"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The /models command lists configured model profiles, and /models <name> switches the active profile."},{"claim_ids":["clm_4b7b754c0f0e3292dda630170bf04de8fa048a7ad9ce165ac5a154bc8a52908c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Self-verification (running tests, compiling, loading the page) is instilled by the system prompt as a habit rather than a blocking gate; when a check cannot run, the agent reports 'unverified:' instead of pretending success."},{"claim_ids":["clm_684300096fdef39891470e9b9b7cbcd1718f7cd06b8b0b6f8716605eda7c3eb8"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README warns that the agent runs model-generated shell commands with full filesystem access and recommends running it inside sandboxes such as devcontainers or isolated VMs."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6d65741c07a4ebb1b146c5b58bde38272e132c77810c32373f05e176f6784b9f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"On Windows the bash tool requires a POSIX shell (/bin/sh), so the agent should be run inside WSL2 or a devcontainer rather than from a bare cmd/PowerShell host."},{"claim_ids":["clm_859bdae9fd107b26ea877b737486d593b395bcf705a276877fdb214df15d0010"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"On first run codehamr seeds .codehamr/config.yaml with a local profile (Ollama, vLLM, LM-Studio) and a hamrpass profile; the system prompt is embedded in the binary, not stored on disk."},{"claim_ids":["clm_975914a3a92def0d0398365969d5760cb849511bb6ab981071432ed73fa3c5ba"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The agent runs a single plain loop: it calls tools until the work is done, then replies, rather than using a more elaborate orchestration scheme."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b4d3375c1a8ab72fe4dc67d439b4a846c9c88e7a60c546a2603234128347dc3e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The agent works with four tools — bash, read_file, write_file, and edit_file — investigating the project directly rather than guessing."},{"claim_ids":["clm_cbf01476c59872491735309e1c80dc42314bd89480d130ddac832fea7d976d21"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Configuration supports OpenAI-compatible endpoints; the example config defines local, openai, and hamrpass profiles with llm and url fields, and the local and openai profiles also carry key and context_size fields."},{"claim_ids":["clm_e76eaafdbf6155822d2ddf78e24f24e3c3e3fad2ccae972dc11d971717dc6055"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project is MIT licensed and open source; HamrPass, a hosted endpoint with tuned model defaults, is optional and will only be built if waitlist demand appears."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f44b5b0405ec7c5b12c29e4b696279af46c3380db6d592b93f5372b7d7f49a5c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The design deliberately favors simplicity: three slash commands, one embedded system prompt, and no router, sub-agents, skill system, or MCP."}],"claim_ids":["clm_06731ae1bf9be4a80775b4297bb526d6fb1627e95041a92d7607ce640c091bd7","clm_1ac704a82a26b8e0a4489f382f603a83766291ab2e253241b2d269c3a8642a83","clm_2175083c3dcb190b435d97a079ae4d1c8d53512ea22eeb5b7e106169d2c8cc18","clm_4b7b754c0f0e3292dda630170bf04de8fa048a7ad9ce165ac5a154bc8a52908c","clm_684300096fdef39891470e9b9b7cbcd1718f7cd06b8b0b6f8716605eda7c3eb8","clm_6d65741c07a4ebb1b146c5b58bde38272e132c77810c32373f05e176f6784b9f","clm_859bdae9fd107b26ea877b737486d593b395bcf705a276877fdb214df15d0010","clm_975914a3a92def0d0398365969d5760cb849511bb6ab981071432ed73fa3c5ba","clm_b4d3375c1a8ab72fe4dc67d439b4a846c9c88e7a60c546a2603234128347dc3e","clm_cbf01476c59872491735309e1c80dc42314bd89480d130ddac832fea7d976d21","clm_e76eaafdbf6155822d2ddf78e24f24e3c3e3fad2ccae972dc11d971717dc6055","clm_f44b5b0405ec7c5b12c29e4b696279af46c3380db6d592b93f5372b7d7f49a5c"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T01:43:04Z","created_by_operation":"op_2ac18e71bbde44e7aa1191650fd2bed7","id":"pg_b0c229ff3af354e1af2dcc6628073dfe","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/codehamr-codehamr-readme-md-8ad8eae6cc57-cc6628073dfe.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_8db6fa9a716e500ca7ac8c89403b0dc6"],"title":"codehamr/codehamr/README.md @ 8ad8eae6cc57","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:43:04Z","updated_by_operation":"op_2ac18e71bbde44e7aa1191650fd2bed7"}
